It is night in Mexico now.
Here in Kochi, it is morning.
My family says bye to me.
"Good night, Maya!" my mother says.
My younger sister Sofía waves her hand happily.
The dog Lola is also with her.
My older brother Diego laughs loudly.
I like his laugh a lot.
I end the call.
I put the phone on a table.
Now there is a great silence in the room.
I look outside the window.
Who is outside?
There is no one there.
I suddenly feel very sad.
There is a photo of my family on the phone.
I look at that photo.
"I am always with you," I say softly.
I miss my home a lot.
